  "evidence": "SwissWatchExpo 63715 original specimen. All 13 original gallery files inspected 17 November 2026; movement 9 reviewed at 1200px from original 2477px file. Bridge visibly stamped 3135 and rotor THIRTY-ONE 31. Case engraving 7 reads 16600 T; original specimen listing identifies base 16600. The T is documented as an observed case marking, not used to create a new alias or infer a universal transition date. Black Sea-Dweller dial, elapsed-time bezel, helium valve side and Oyster bracelet/flip-lock visible. Dealer attributes 2005–2006, 40mm steel case and sapphire crystal; period/materials remain attributions. Dial depth text is visible but does not establish present pressure resistance. No transfer to neighbouring references or other unopened specimens; original fitment, service status, full chronology and user-watch authenticity are not independently established. Existing photographs remain separate specimens. Overall execution/period research remains incomplete.",
